## What this is

__PROJECT_DESCRIPTION__

Each sub-repo is a self-contained git repo in a subfolder. The hub itself is a small git repo that tracks only this `AGENTS.md`, the thin `CLAUDE.md` import, `project.yaml`, `invoke-ai.sh`, `README.md`, and `.gitignore`. The sub-repo directories are listed in the managed block of `.gitignore` so they don't pollute the hub's git history.

## How agents load context

This file (`AGENTS.md` at the hub root) is the canonical, agent-neutral project map. The hub's `CLAUDE.md` is a thin `@AGENTS.md` import kept for compatibility — never put content there.

- **Claude Code** — `./invoke-ai.sh` (agent `claude`) launches with `--add-dir` for every sub-repo present locally; Claude auto-loads this file plus each mounted sub-repo's context file.
- **omp** — finds this file by walking up from the current directory; it has no `--add-dir`, so sub-repo context files are NOT auto-loaded.

When working inside `<sub-repo>/`, read `<sub-repo>/AGENTS.md` first — runtimes without multi-dir auto-load (omp) do not load it automatically.

Per-repo rules live in the repo they apply to: each sub-repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` (plus a thin `CLAUDE.md` import). Edit `acme-app/AGENTS.md` for app-specific conventions, etc.

