## Working with this hub

- `./invoke-ai.sh` — pick an agent (claude, omp, …) and launch it from the hub
- `/ws-hub-repos clone` — clone every registered repo URL into a missing subfolder
- `/ws-hub-repos pull` — `git pull` across all sub-repos
- `/ws-hub-status` — aggregated git status across all sub-repos
- `/ws-hub-add-repo --scan` — detect un-registered sub-repos
- `/ws-hub-add-repo` — register a new sub-repo (clone or adopt)
- `/ws-hub-describe` — refresh sub-repo descriptions from their READMEs

## Documentation

Product-level documentation lives in the `role: docs` sub-repo (see
`project.yaml`): user docs (`docs/`, synced to Outline) and cross-repo
dev docs (`dev-docs/` — product ADRs, architecture, client materials).
Write product-level docs THERE, not in the hub and not in feature repos.
Repo-specific dev docs stay in each sub-repo's own `dev-docs/`.

## Access notes

Sub-repos you don't have git access to will simply be missing from disk and `invoke-ai.sh` will skip them with a warning. The hub itself contains no sensitive code — it's a meta repo, safe to share broadly.

Hub conventions are documented in `.claude/skills/project-hub-conventions/SKILL.md` (vendored locally — works without the ws-marketplace plugin installed).
